      "sample_index": 1,
      "text": "To find the smallest four-digit number divisible by $33$, we need to identify the smallest four-digit number and then determine the smallest multiple of $33$ that is greater than or equal to that number.\n\nThe smallest four-digit number is $1000$. We are looking for the smallest multiple of $33$ that is greater than or equal to $1000$. To find this, we can divide $1000$ by $33$ and then round up to the next whole number, because we need the smallest multiple that is greater than or equal to $1000$.\n\nFirst, we perform the division:\n\n\\[\n1000 \\div 33 \\approx 30.303\n\\]\n\nSince we need a whole number, we round $30.303$ up to $31$. This means the smallest multiple of $33$ that is greater than or equal to $1000$ is:\n\n\\[\n33 \\times 31 = 1023\n\\]\n\nTherefore, the smallest four-digit number that is divisible by $33$ is:\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{1023}\n\\]",
